        "description": "<img src=\"https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/strauss-zelnick-gta-take-two.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp\" /> <p>Take-Two's latest financials are in, and they come with a few surprises. First off, Take-Two CEO Strauss Zelnick has confirmed that the publisher's sales are mostly digital, in response to <a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/sony-ending-playstation-discs-physical-media-january-2028\">Sony's controversial decision to stop manufacturing physical disc-based games</a>. \"Our business is well over 90% digitally distributed,\" he said during the call (thanks, <a href=\"https://bsky.app/profile/jasonschreier.bsky.social/post/3msilkyu2ic2q\">Jason Schreier</a>). \"It's already a digital business.\"</p> <p><a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/take-two-stock-digital-gta6-physical\">Read more</a></p>",
